WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.500
- Good morning, Believe Nation!

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.133
Today's message is fight for your beliefs.

00:00:05.133 --> 00:00:07.359
Over to you Marco Pierre White.

00:00:07.359 --> 00:00:09.250
(rooster crowing)

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:12.425
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:12.425 --> 00:00:14.734
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:00:14.734 --> 00:00:18.234
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:19.075 --> 00:00:20.841
- Many people have condemned
me for being controversial.

00:00:20.841 --> 00:00:25.108
- Many people have condemned
me for being controversial.

00:00:25.108 --> 00:00:27.738
I was never controversial.

00:00:27.738 --> 00:00:31.238
As I've always said, most of my reputation

00:00:32.293 --> 00:00:35.783
is a product of
exaggeration and ignorance.

00:00:35.783 --> 00:00:37.014
Did I shout?

00:00:37.014 --> 00:00:37.931
Yes, I did.

00:00:38.990 --> 00:00:40.274
But I led from the front.

00:00:40.274 --> 00:00:42.180
I nailed my colors to the mast.

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:44.024
I fought for my profession.

00:00:44.024 --> 00:00:45.349
If you're going to be a rebel,

00:00:45.349 --> 00:00:46.678
make sure you win.

00:00:46.678 --> 00:00:48.639
If you're going to be a revolutionary,

00:00:48.639 --> 00:00:51.433
then fight for what you truly believe in.

00:00:51.433 --> 00:00:53.577
And that's all I ever did.

00:00:53.577 --> 00:00:55.558
And the boys behind me they followed me.

00:00:55.558 --> 00:00:57.728
- Most people don't
know what they stand for

00:00:57.728 --> 00:01:00.061
and so they don't know
what they're fighting for.

00:01:00.061 --> 00:01:01.717
Most people are lost

00:01:01.717 --> 00:01:03.075
and that's why they end up following

00:01:03.075 --> 00:01:05.095
somebody who has more certainty

00:01:05.095 --> 00:01:07.830
who has more self-awareness than they do,

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:09.859
instead of living their own life.

00:01:09.859 --> 00:01:11.913
Instead of being a leader for yourself,

00:01:11.913 --> 00:01:13.200
you're following somebody else

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:15.633
who just has more confidence
and self-awareness.

00:01:15.633 --> 00:01:18.799
You need to know what you stand for

00:01:18.799 --> 00:01:21.589
to know what you're fighting for.

00:01:21.589 --> 00:01:23.360
This is why I wrote the book

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:25.975
and not some promotional piece here.

00:01:25.975 --> 00:01:27.632
It's super important,

00:01:27.632 --> 00:01:30.170
is identify what is the one thing

00:01:30.170 --> 00:01:31.786
that you will not compromise?

00:01:31.786 --> 00:01:35.914
What is the one most
important core value to you?

00:01:35.914 --> 00:01:37.735
Most people don't know,

00:01:37.735 --> 00:01:39.193
and if you don't know

00:01:39.193 --> 00:01:40.612
then how are you living a life

00:01:40.612 --> 00:01:43.300
and running a business
with any kind of purpose?

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:44.681
You'll just be constantly reacting

00:01:44.681 --> 00:01:46.617
to what other people are giving you.

00:01:46.617 --> 00:01:48.350
You're living somebody else's life

00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:49.681
and not your own.

00:01:49.681 --> 00:01:50.983
And so I think that self-awareness

00:01:50.983 --> 00:01:52.177
is one of the most important things

00:01:52.177 --> 00:01:53.095
that you could have

00:01:53.095 --> 00:01:55.637
not just as an entrepreneur
but as a human being.

00:01:55.637 --> 00:01:57.506
For you to know what your one word is,

00:01:57.506 --> 00:01:59.003
for you to know what your one single

00:01:59.003 --> 00:02:00.592
most important core value is

00:02:00.592 --> 00:02:03.630
that becomes the lens through
which you see the world.

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:06.727
Now you can proactively build a business

00:02:06.727 --> 00:02:08.617
and proactively create a life

00:02:08.617 --> 00:02:11.958
that reflects your most
important core value.

00:02:11.958 --> 00:02:13.688
Now you know what to fight for.

00:02:13.688 --> 00:02:16.630
Now you know what you're no
longer willing to accept.

00:02:16.630 --> 00:02:18.664
Because you've always
shown these tendencies.

00:02:18.664 --> 00:02:21.367
You always gravitated
towards this one word,

00:02:21.367 --> 00:02:22.355
this one core value.

00:02:22.355 --> 00:02:24.708
But it was always haphazard.

00:02:24.708 --> 00:02:26.982
It was always when things come up.

00:02:26.982 --> 00:02:28.498
It was always random.

00:02:28.498 --> 00:02:31.653
And so what are the chances
that that perfect mentor

00:02:31.653 --> 00:02:33.001
or guide or relationship

00:02:33.001 --> 00:02:36.377
or business opportunity is
going to just fall on your lap?

00:02:36.377 --> 00:02:40.400
It could happen but
it's a small percentage.

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:43.199
Where now if you purposely are setting out

00:02:43.199 --> 00:02:45.678
to build a business and a life

00:02:45.678 --> 00:02:47.799
around your most important core value

00:02:47.799 --> 00:02:51.317
that percentage is going
to dramatically explode.

00:02:51.317 --> 00:02:54.819
Now, you're no longer
willing to be around people

00:02:54.819 --> 00:02:58.674
who don't share the values that you do.

00:02:58.674 --> 00:03:00.761
Now you're not going to be with people

00:03:00.761 --> 00:03:02.479
who pound down your ideas.

00:03:02.479 --> 00:03:03.428
Who tell you all the reasons

00:03:03.428 --> 00:03:05.482
why you're not going to be successful.

00:03:05.482 --> 00:03:07.711
Now you're going to be
open to opportunities

00:03:07.711 --> 00:03:09.437
and they're going to find you.

00:03:09.437 --> 00:03:11.692
That support you in doing great things.

00:03:11.692 --> 00:03:14.902
Most people though haven't figured it out.

00:03:14.902 --> 00:03:16.342
Most people won't figure it out

00:03:16.342 --> 00:03:19.052
and that's why most people
will not be great leaders.

00:03:19.052 --> 00:03:21.720
That's why most people will
never build a great life.

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:23.740
That's why most people walk around

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:27.509
feeling like they could be
doing so much more in their life

00:03:27.509 --> 00:03:29.226
and they're not even coming close

00:03:29.226 --> 00:03:30.861
to reaching their potential.

00:03:30.861 --> 00:03:32.427
Doesn't mean you have
to be down in the dumps,

00:03:32.427 --> 00:03:34.620
doesn't mean you have to had no success.

00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:36.451
There's lots of people
who had plenty of success

00:03:36.451 --> 00:03:39.109
but they know that they
could be doing more.

00:03:39.109 --> 00:03:41.464
They know that they're
nowhere close to their ceiling

00:03:41.464 --> 00:03:43.344
and they don't know how to get there.

00:03:43.344 --> 00:03:44.312
And they don't know what's wrong.

00:03:44.312 --> 00:03:46.661
What's wrong is you don't
know what you stand for.

00:03:46.661 --> 00:03:48.626
What's wrong is you don't
know what you're fighting for.

00:03:48.626 --> 00:03:50.347
What's wrong is you're
just following other people

00:03:50.347 --> 00:03:53.748
instead of being the leader
that you were meant to be.

00:03:53.748 --> 00:03:55.162
So find your one word.

00:03:55.162 --> 00:03:58.748
Find your single most important core value

00:03:58.748 --> 00:04:01.913
and then you've found what
you should be fighting for.

00:04:01.913 --> 00:04:03.600
So the question of the
day today is, I'm curious.

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:04.900
What is your one word?

00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:07.206
What is the single most important thing

00:04:07.206 --> 00:04:08.771
that you are fighting for?

00:04:08.771 --> 00:04:11.144
I want the one word and
I want a sentence or two

00:04:11.144 --> 00:04:13.663
as to why it really
means something to you.

00:04:13.663 --> 00:04:15.229
Why is this so important to you?

00:04:15.229 --> 00:04:17.947
Leave it in the comments and
we'll join in the discussion.

00:04:17.947 --> 00:04:19.958
I also want to give a
quick shout out to David.

00:04:19.958 --> 00:04:20.791
David, thank you so much

00:04:20.791 --> 00:04:23.020
for picking up a copy of
my book, Your One Word.

00:04:23.020 --> 00:04:25.313
I really really really
appreciate the support

00:04:25.313 --> 00:04:26.819
and hope you're enjoying it.

00:04:26.819 --> 00:04:28.538
Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:04:28.538 --> 00:04:29.613
I believe in you.

00:04:29.613 --> 00:04:31.221
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself.

00:04:31.221 --> 00:04:33.242
And whatever your one word is,

00:04:33.242 --> 00:04:35.759
much love and I'll see
you again tomorrow morning

00:04:35.759 --> 00:04:38.354
for another shot of Entspresso.

00:04:38.354 --> 00:04:40.627
♫ I wake up every morning

00:04:40.627 --> 00:04:44.633
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:04:44.633 --> 00:04:45.541
Hey, Believe Nation.

00:04:45.541 --> 00:04:46.963
Thank you so much for watching.

00:04:46.963 --> 00:04:48.968
If you want to learn
more about this subject,

00:04:48.968 --> 00:04:50.416
get a little bit deeper on it.

00:04:50.416 --> 00:04:52.106
I'm going to share some extra bonus clips

00:04:52.106 --> 00:04:53.619
that I hope you'll enjoy.

00:04:53.619 --> 00:04:56.382
- And what I'm telling artists
is you got to have balls

00:04:56.382 --> 00:04:57.913
and got to let these guys know.

00:04:57.913 --> 00:04:59.379
If you're a DJ be DJ.

00:04:59.379 --> 00:05:02.308
If you're a radio personality,
be a radio personality

00:05:02.308 --> 00:05:03.539
and nothing more.

00:05:03.539 --> 00:05:05.224
We make the music that allows them

00:05:05.224 --> 00:05:06.611
to have a voice on the radio.

00:05:06.611 --> 00:05:08.803
And they took control and try to say,

00:05:08.803 --> 00:05:10.382
say that they have all the power

00:05:10.382 --> 00:05:12.595
and going to dictate what we have to do.

00:05:12.595 --> 00:05:13.723
I spoke out against it.

00:05:13.723 --> 00:05:15.904
So they got a dummy to go up there

00:05:15.904 --> 00:05:17.107
and be a dummy on the radio

00:05:17.107 --> 00:05:20.182
and speak on their
behalf and talk about me.

00:05:20.182 --> 00:05:23.235
And it's really unfortunate
'cause they're using him

00:05:23.235 --> 00:05:25.428
and he's not even a part of my fight.

00:05:25.428 --> 00:05:26.600
My fight is a big fight.

00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:28.503
My fight is against any power structure

00:05:28.503 --> 00:05:31.205
that's going to try to hold
back the freedom of speech.

00:05:31.205 --> 00:05:33.361
And that fight ain't over yet.

00:05:33.361 --> 00:05:36.553
- Amazed at how few people
have a belief system.

00:05:36.553 --> 00:05:39.303
What do they actually believe in?

00:05:42.524 --> 00:05:46.480
And, yeah, it's okay to offend you guys.

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:50.099
90% of you will do what's expected of you

00:05:50.099 --> 00:05:52.932
as opposed to what you want to do.

00:05:53.811 --> 00:05:57.288
And I even, when I come
to an event like this say

00:05:57.288 --> 00:05:58.357
why am I here?

00:05:58.357 --> 00:06:01.999
Why would I even bother to take
an hour of my valuable time?

00:06:01.999 --> 00:06:03.671
(audience laughing)

00:06:03.671 --> 00:06:04.977
No, it's true.

00:06:04.977 --> 00:06:07.478
I have to have a purpose.

00:06:07.478 --> 00:06:08.630
My goal is very simple.

00:06:08.630 --> 00:06:11.025
If I can convert one of you.

00:06:11.025 --> 00:06:13.668
There's probably 400, 500 people here.

00:06:13.668 --> 00:06:16.382
If I can convert one of
you to follow your belief

00:06:16.382 --> 00:06:20.514
and have the guts to follow your belief,

00:06:20.514 --> 00:06:23.597
I'll think of the hour as well spent.

00:06:24.639 --> 00:06:27.620
So, I would say, what am
I trying to do and why?

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:28.453
I don't speak because somebody will write

00:06:28.453 --> 00:06:31.347
I don't speak because somebody will write

00:06:31.347 --> 00:06:33.097
nice things about it.

00:06:34.086 --> 00:06:35.902
I always sort of have a purpose,

00:06:35.902 --> 00:06:38.057
but I have a belief system.

00:06:38.057 --> 00:06:41.235
And most people, even
successful companies,

00:06:41.235 --> 00:06:43.036
And most people, even
successful companies,

00:06:43.036 --> 00:06:45.582
and I have big beef with Fortune 500 CEOs

00:06:45.582 --> 00:06:46.857
I can talk about.

00:06:46.857 --> 00:06:50.523
There's very little leadership there,

00:06:50.523 --> 00:06:54.420
don't have an internal compass
of what they believe in.

00:06:54.420 --> 00:06:57.221
It's what do others expect.

00:06:57.221 --> 00:07:00.900
You know when I graduated, I
went into entrepreneurship.

00:07:00.900 --> 00:07:02.753
Nobody went into entrepreneurship

00:07:02.753 --> 00:07:03.875
out of the business school.

00:07:03.875 --> 00:07:05.276
And people said why wouldn't you

00:07:05.276 --> 00:07:07.683
work for Goldman or McKinsey?

00:07:07.683 --> 00:07:09.766
And I said why would you?

00:07:11.010 --> 00:07:15.947
I couldn't fathom why you
would want to do that job.

00:07:15.947 --> 00:07:18.788
Right? I still can't, by the way.

00:07:18.788 --> 00:07:21.788
(audience laughing)

00:07:22.941 --> 00:07:24.973
For those of you going to those places,

00:07:24.973 --> 00:07:26.652
and I'm sure there's plenty,

00:07:26.652 --> 00:07:29.960
I'm probably not the right
person to talk to you.

00:07:29.960 --> 00:07:31.882
I frankly don't even care to talk to you.

00:07:31.882 --> 00:07:33.032
All of you others.

00:07:33.032 --> 00:07:36.032
(audience laughing)

00:07:37.283 --> 00:07:39.737
I think there's something
wrong with anybody

00:07:39.737 --> 00:07:41.466
who fundamentally wants to go work for

00:07:41.466 --> 00:07:43.654
one of the consultants or
the investment banks today

00:07:43.654 --> 00:07:45.117
and there's probably,

00:07:45.117 --> 00:07:48.737
they don't understand how
the world is going to work

00:07:48.737 --> 00:07:50.117
in the future.

00:07:50.117 --> 00:07:53.156
But my point again is,
have a belief system.

00:07:53.156 --> 00:07:55.102
Follow that compass.

00:07:55.102 --> 00:07:56.878
And I'm overstating it a bit.

00:07:56.878 --> 00:08:00.379
So there may be some hope
for those of you going there.

00:08:00.379 --> 00:08:03.738
But it's only a little
bit of an exaggeration.

00:08:03.738 --> 00:08:06.674
But it's only a little
bit of an exaggeration.

00:08:06.674 --> 00:08:10.362
Let me go back to this
issue of Fortune 500 CEOs.

00:08:10.362 --> 00:08:13.568
I've talked to many over the years.

00:08:13.568 --> 00:08:16.950
If a New York Times
writer writes an article,

00:08:16.950 --> 00:08:21.062
they want to change their
strategy, they want to respond.

00:08:21.062 --> 00:08:24.104
How silly is that, that some English major

00:08:24.104 --> 00:08:26.354
who's never had a business job

00:08:26.354 --> 00:08:30.125
can determine the strategy
of a Fortune 500 company?

00:08:30.125 --> 00:08:32.120
Why? Because they care
about what's written

00:08:32.120 --> 00:08:35.486
not what their belief system is.

00:08:35.486 --> 00:08:38.071
Do you know what Elon Musk
would say to that writer?

00:08:38.071 --> 00:08:39.571
Go get a real job.

00:08:41.835 --> 00:08:43.603
What Jeff Bezos would say?

00:08:43.603 --> 00:08:44.832
That's leadership.

00:08:44.832 --> 00:08:46.559
Having a belief system.

00:08:46.559 --> 00:08:49.553
Knowing what's driving
you to do what you do.

00:08:49.553 --> 00:08:54.154
Not you're fitting in to
do career enhancement.

00:08:54.154 --> 00:08:56.965
Or, making it look good to somebody else

00:08:56.965 --> 00:09:00.955
whether it's to your
friends, or to your boss,

00:09:00.955 --> 00:09:01.788
or to shareholders.

00:09:01.788 --> 00:09:04.139
or to shareholders.

00:09:04.139 --> 00:09:07.325
And frankly, you look at all the companies

00:09:07.325 --> 00:09:09.330
that are languishing in the Valley,

00:09:09.330 --> 00:09:10.770
the older companies.

00:09:10.770 --> 00:09:13.539
They generally don't have a belief system.

00:09:13.539 --> 00:09:16.662
They're generally trying to
meet some quarterly target,

00:09:16.662 --> 00:09:19.364
without saying, here's
how we will be different

00:09:19.364 --> 00:09:22.428
and here's how we'll do it.

00:09:22.428 --> 00:09:25.589
Apple did languish for 10, 15 years,

00:09:25.589 --> 00:09:28.748
and then Steve Jobs came
in with a point of view,

00:09:28.748 --> 00:09:31.408
and created the most valuable
company in the world.

00:09:31.408 --> 00:09:33.049
He did irrational things.

00:09:33.049 --> 00:09:34.132
If you go back to January of 2007,

00:09:34.132 --> 00:09:37.029
If you go back to January of 2007,

00:09:37.029 --> 00:09:38.985
January 1, everybody was saying

00:09:38.985 --> 00:09:41.828
nobody wants a phone without a keyboard.

00:09:41.828 --> 00:09:44.832
Nobody wants a phone that costs $699.

00:09:44.832 --> 00:09:46.779
I can go on with the litany.

00:09:46.779 --> 00:09:49.531
Those were all English
majors writing articles.

00:09:49.531 --> 00:09:52.289
I have this beef against English majors

00:09:52.289 --> 00:09:53.418
(audience laughing)

00:09:53.418 --> 00:09:55.083
Not all English majors are bad

00:09:55.083 --> 00:09:59.233
but the majority of them
at Stanford are undirected

00:09:59.233 --> 00:10:01.083
and don't have a goal or a purpose.

00:10:01.083 --> 00:10:02.841
(audience laughing)

00:10:02.841 --> 00:10:03.674
Sorry.

00:10:05.970 --> 00:10:07.361
And that's not to say,

00:10:07.361 --> 00:10:09.213
among them there isn't 20%

00:10:09.213 --> 00:10:10.616
that are really good.

00:10:10.616 --> 00:10:12.519
They just didn't get the right guidance

00:10:12.519 --> 00:10:14.152
and ended up in the wrong place.

00:10:14.152 --> 00:10:15.414
(audience laughing)

00:10:15.414 --> 00:10:17.747
I like purposeful education.

